solution:
Sample space when two coins are tossed: {HH, HT, TH, TT}
Total outcomes = \(4\)
Favorable outcomes for exactly one head: {HT, TH}
Number of favorable outcomes = \(2\)
Probability = \(\frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2}\)

Sample space: {HH, HT, TH, TT}
At least one head means one or more heads
Favorable outcomes: {HH, HT, TH}
Probability = \(\frac{3}{4}\)
Alternatively, P(at least one head) = \(1 - P(\text{no heads}) = 1 - \frac{1}{4} = \frac{3}{4}\)

Sample space: {HH, HT, TH, TT}
At most one head means zero heads OR one head
Favorable outcomes: {HT, TH, TT}
Number of favorable outcomes = \(3\)
Probability = \(\frac{3}{4}\)

Sample space: {HH, HT, TH, TT}
Same face outcomes: {HH, TT}
Number of favorable outcomes = \(2\)
Probability = \(\frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2}\)

Let A = first coin shows head, B = exactly two heads appear
Outcomes with exactly two heads: {HHT, HTH, THH}
Outcomes where first coin is head AND exactly two heads: {HHT, HTH}
P(A|B) = \(\frac{\text{Number of outcomes in } A ∩ B}{\text{Number of outcomes in } B} = \frac{2}{3}\)

Sample space: {HHH, HHT, HTH, HTT, THH, THT, TTH, TTT}
No two consecutive coins show same face: alternating pattern
Favorable outcomes: {HTH, THT}
Number of favorable outcomes = \(2\)
Probability = \(\frac{2}{8} = \frac{1}{4}\)

Let A = third coin shows head, B = at least two heads appear
Outcomes with at least two heads: {HHH, HHT, HTH, THH}
Outcomes where third coin is head AND at least two heads: {HHH, HTH, THH}
P(A|B) = \(\frac{\text{Number of outcomes in } A ∩ B}{\text{Number of outcomes in } B} = \frac{3}{4}\)
